# Deterministic fuse check for the print-in-place piano hinge. Unlike the
# living-hinge designs this check was built for, there is NO flexure web to
# excuse: the three bodies (leaf A, leaf B, free pin) are joined only through
# clearances, so a healthy assembly is THREE disjoint shells in the sliced
# STL and no flexure zone needs dropping — count them directly. A pin welded
# to any bore (clear_xy lost) or a leaf welded to a leaf (leaf_gap lost)
# reads as fewer bodies, which is a STRONG WARN for reviewer signoff.
assert pip-piano-hinge.stl 3

# Mandatory negative control: part="fused" drives an oversized pin through
# every bore, welding the whole assembly into one solid. It must STAY one
# body — proving the check can fire (and that no over-generous zone is
# masking a real fuse by splitting the control too).
control fused 1
